<speak>That order works for the conversation. I have a habit of trying to complete every page before moving on, even when the information is better considered together. My business team has started sending meeting papers as a collection of clearly marked sections, and I find that easier than a continuous narrative. It also makes it possible to leave a section alone and return to it without feeling that I have lost the thread. I am trying to be less attached to doing everything in precisely the same sequence.</speak>